WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.009
When talking about the world’s 1.6 billion
Muslims, American presidents are traditionally

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:09.780
very careful to differentiate between the
vast majority who practice the religion peacefully

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.089
and the small minority who don't.

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:18.590
There's nothing in there, in Islam that condones
the kind of brutality that we've seen

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:25.830
Our actions today were not aimed against Islam,
the faith of hundreds of millions of good,

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.830
peace-loving people.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:32.970
We are not at war with Islam, we are at war
with those who have perverted Islam.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.400
President Donald Trump has not continued this
tradition.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.940
Do you think Islam is at war with The West?

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.780
I think Islam hates us.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:46.940
There’s something, there's something there
that’s a tremendous hatred.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.620
To understand why Trump is breaking with his
predecessors, you have to understand his chief

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.400
strategist, Steve Bannon.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.250
Before he joined the Trump campaign, Bannon
ran the far-right website Breitbart, where

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.180
he hosted a daily radio show.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.720
The face of terror is not the true faith of
Islam.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.840
Islam is peace.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.060
If you listen to Bannon's radio show, and
watch his speeches, you start to get a sense

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.400
of how he sees the world.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.540
Bannon believes that the US and Western Europe
are in the middle of an historical struggle

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.160
against Islam itself.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.500
Bannon isn’t talking about the American
founding fathers, he’s talking about European

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:01.810
leaders who fought off Muslim conquests in
the 8th and 16th centuries.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:05.060
That is the context in which Bannon approaches
policy today

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:10.229
This context also helps us understand Bannon's
views about refugees from the muslim world.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:15.390
In a 2015 interview, Bannon and then-Representative
Ryan Zinke of Montana discussed Obama’s

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.440
plan to take in10,000 refugees from Syria.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:57.220
Bannon seems to think Syrian refugees are
incapable of adapting to the American way

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.220
of life.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:11.470
Before Breitbart, Bannon made documentary
films.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:16.280
In the outline for one film, which he didn't
end up making, Bannon warns of an Islamist

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.380
takeover of the United States.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:22.120
The opening scene features the call to prayer
and a flag of the Muslim star and crescent

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.900
flying over the U.S. capitol building.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:35.560
Though his current focus is on Muslims, Bannon
has expressed a desire to keep all foreign-born

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:37.060
people out of the U.S.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.060
In a 2015 interview, he disagreed when Donald Trump

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.420
said we should keep high-skilled immigrants in the US.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:10.040
Less than 14% of Silicon
Valley CEOs are Asian.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:15.840
But the fake statistic supports his view:
that legal immigrants are just as problematic

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.560
if not more, than those who are here illegally.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.580
The number is closer to 13 percent, but Bannon’s
point is that

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:45.689
immigrants somehow make America less American.

00:04:45.689 --> 00:04:50.889
He believes they don’t share American values,
and that, even when here legally, they take jobs

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:52.949
away from native-born Americans.

00:04:52.949 --> 00:04:57.190
And, in this view, Bannon is way out of sync
with mainstream Republicans,

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.740
who, along with business interests like the
Chamber of Commerce, have long said they welcome

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.330
legal immigrants.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:06.240
We're gonna need more legal immigration.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.029
Immigrants are an economic engine of vitality
for our country, they make things happen.

00:05:11.029 --> 00:05:13.889
We need to figure out how to have more legal
immigration.

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:15.020
Immigrants are the lifeblood of our society.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:20.259
I think probably, you know, the most dedicated
Americans are those who come here as immigrants.

00:05:20.259 --> 00:05:24.759
Bannon blames legal immigrants for what he
describes as a bleak economic landscape for

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:26.460
native-born Americans.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:32.300
If you’re under 30 years old, your children
are going to be poor, and your grandchildren

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.069
are going to be paupers.

00:05:34.069 --> 00:05:38.569
The only way to stop this from happening,
Bannon says, is to rise up against those whom

00:05:38.569 --> 00:05:43.839
he calls the ruling political class, those
who allow immigration, legal and illegal,

00:05:43.839 --> 00:05:45.210
to continue.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.210
Think about it.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.020
If the elites are so good, how did we get
in this jam?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:52.629
This is the fourth great crisis in American
history: we had the Revolution, we had the

00:05:52.629 --> 00:05:56.659
Civil War, we had the Great Depression and
World War II, this is the great fourth turning

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:57.720
in American history

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:01.160
Bannon’s views have already started to influence policy.

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:05.030
Multiple news outlets have confirmed that
he was behind the executive order temporarily

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:10.610
banning travelers from 7 majority-muslim countries
and almost all refugees from entering the

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:11.610
US.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:16.480
A federal judge has temporarily halted the
ban, but with the president’s ear, and a

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:20.979
seat on the National Security Council,
Bannon's vision of a closed America, at war

00:06:20.979 --> 00:06:24.039
with Islam will continue to influence policy.

